  "description": "<p>See: <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/json-ld/#flattened-document-form\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://www.w3.org/TR/json-ld/#flattened-document-form</a></p>\n\n<p>The response from a request with this header: -H\"Accept: application/ld+json; profile=\\\"http://www.w3.org/ns/json-ld#flattened\\\"\"</p>\n\n<p>does not return the flattened JSON-LD profile. Instead, it returns the expanded JSON-LD profile. This is likely a problem with the underlying serialization library and may be solved with this issue: \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-2242\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-2242\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Remove dependency on OpenRDF\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10300?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-2242\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n.</p>",
